@startuml friends-sequence
title Send a Friend Request — search, validation and persistence
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
autonumber
actor Sender
boundary "Sender client" as Client
control "Friend service" as Service
database "Request store" as Store
note over Sender, Store
  Precondition: sender is authenticated.
  Search: case-insensitive username substring; exclude sender.
  Hidden/blocked-user policies remain unresolved.
end note
loop Search / revise until recipient selected or sender cancels
  Sender -> Client: Enter or revise query
  Client -> Service: Search users(query)
  Service --> Client: Matching users or empty result
  Client --> Sender: Display results or no results
end
alt Cancel search, selection or send confirmation
  Sender -> Client: Cancel
  Client --> Sender: Return without sending
else Select recipient and confirm sending
  Sender -> Client: Select recipient; confirm send
  Client -> Service: Send friend request(recipient)
  Service -> Service: Validate self / friendship / pending direction
  alt Self, already friends, or outgoing pending request
    Service --> Client: Reject with reason; no new request
    Client --> Sender: Display rejection, not success
  else Incoming pending request exists
    Service --> Client: Return existing incoming request; do not send another
    Client --> Sender: Show incoming request with Accept / Decline
    note right of Client: End send goal; handling incoming request is separate.
  else Eligible recipient
    Service -> Store: Store pending request; enforce one per account pair
    alt Save successful
      Store --> Service: Confirm stored and available to recipient
      Service --> Client: Confirm request sent (pending)
      Client --> Sender: Display confirmed pending request
    else Save failed
      Store --> Service: Save failure
      Service --> Client: Report failure, not success
      Client --> Sender: Display failure
    end
  end
end
note over Sender, Store
  Sending alone never creates friendship; acceptance/decline is separate.
  Self is rejected by the service even though search excludes sender.
  A missing response is not a confirmed rejection or save failure.
  Without confirmation the client must not claim success; recovery is unresolved.
end note
@enduml
